  "body": "`machining3d/{entry,feed,ladder,shell}.rs`, `multiaxis/rough.rs` and `quality` use `Dexel::block`, `subtract_upright`, `engagement` and `mask` directly. Only `engagement_on(&Columns)` goes through the seam. Depends on (2/6).\n\nPart of #26 (retire the column engine). Research and consumer map: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/26#issuecomment-6754685656\n\nThe step is behaviour-neutral: `stock_engine_agreement` and the goldens stay byte-identical where verdicts are.\n\nDone means: camcraft-motion uses no `Dexel` outside tests, and the finish3d, rough and quality goldens are byte-identical.\n",
